            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0745" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.796/293: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-08T17:00:00-05:00">October 8, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>238. From Currie. Your despatch no. 113, September 3, 1941.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d773-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Mr. T. V. Soong has provided me with written assurance that the DC–3 transport
                    planes which are to be procured through Lease-Lend will be operated by China
                    National Aviation Corporation personnel for the Government of China.
                    [Currie.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
